of an existential question I think what happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:56.560
is Serendipity either happens or it doesn't&nbsp;
happen to you I don't think it's like falling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:04.920
in love you can try your best to make something&nbsp;
happen in your love life say but if it's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:11.160
to happen there's this ineffable thing called&nbsp;
chemistry which allows it to happen and I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:18.240
the same kind of operating principles relate to&nbsp;
Serendipity in your life sure I got a great gal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.080
for you she's studying to do this and then you&nbsp;
meet the person and it's not there's nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:30.120
there and then right the person who's totally&nbsp;
wrong for you and yeah it happens right do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:38.320
think an artist can hurt themselves in some sense&nbsp;
or their career by not believing in Serendipity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:47.120
well I mean I can't speak for other people but&nbsp;
I believe that whatever you you believe you put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:57.200
out into the universe okay sort of a karmic thing&nbsp;
so if if you're open to serendipitous good things&nbsp;&nbsp;

